    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made it a returned field.\n\n**What `identityKey` is:** `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`. A new owner is rejected with **409 Conflict only when its whole `identityKey` equals an existing owner's**.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived `getIdentityKey()` that builds the key from the already-normalized stored fields. MapStruct auto-maps it into the DTO by name (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`).\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes and returns it.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Removed the three separate duplicate rules (`rejectWhenTelephoneInUse`, `rejectWhenEmailInUse`, and the `DuplicateHouseholdException` rejection in `applyHouseholdMembership`), plus the now-unused `isTelephoneInUse` / `isValueInUseByExistingOwner` helpers.\n   - Added a single `rejectWhenIdentityInUse(owner)` that compares the owner's whole `identityKey` against all existing owners.\n   - Ordered it **after** household resolution so the key sees the final `householdId`. `applyHouseholdMembership` still assigns the shared `householdId` on opt-in, but sharing a household is no longer a rejection on its own.\n\n4. **`rest/advice/`** \u2014 added `DuplicateIdentityException` (a `OwnerConflictException` \u2192 409) and removed the now-dead `DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateEmailException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException`; updated the stale javadoc in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n\n**Behaviour change (as specified):** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different `identityKey`s and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit log confirms the collision path (`An owner with identity key +61400000004|| already exists` \u2192 409).",
